<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFramework>netstandard2.0</TargetFramework>
		<ApplicationIcon>images\AcumaticaRESTClientLogo.ico</ApplicationIcon>
		<Version>6.0.2-preview</Version>
		<Company>Acumatica</Company>
		<Description>A simple client allowing to use Acumatica REST API from C#. </Description>
		<Copyright>Acumatica</Copyright>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Acumatica/AcumaticaRESTAPIClientForCSharp</PackageProjectUrl>
		<PackageIcon>AcumaticaRESTClientLogo.png</PackageIcon>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/Acumatica/AcumaticaRESTAPIClientForCSharp</RepositoryUrl>
		<PackageTags>Acumatica;REST;client;</PackageTags>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>
6.0.2-preview

BREAKING CHANGES compared to 6.0.1-preview (OAuth 2.0 authorization code flow):
- Authorize and AuthorizeAsync no longer take clientSecret or usePost. Use responseMode (Query, Fragment or FormPost; the default is Query) instead of usePost. The optional parameters are in the order responseType, responseMode, codeChallenge, nonce, state.
- ResponseType values changed (IdToken = 1, Token = 2). IdToken and Token can now be requested independently, so 'code token' is possible.
- The auth/login endpoint support is removed: Login and LoginAsync no longer exist. Use the OAuth 2.0 methods, or the Acumatica.RESTClient.NonProductionLogin package for non-production sites.

NEW:
- PKCE support: pass codeChallenge to Authorize and codeVerifier when receiving the token.
- Nonce support: pass nonce to Authorize and expectedNonce when receiving the token; it is verified against the ID token.
- State support: pass state to Authorize and expectedState when receiving the token; a mismatch is rejected.
- ReceiveAccessTokenAuthCode and ReceiveAccessTokenAuthCodeAsync can take the callback Uri. The authorization code is extracted from it and errors returned by Acumatica are reported.
- Added the ResponseMode enum and the Token.Id_token property.
- VersionAndEndpoints.Features lists the features enabled on the instance (returned by the root endpoint starting with 26R2).
- XML documentation for the OAuth methods and the Token class. Overloads with the same description now inherit it (inheritdoc).
		</PackageReleaseNotes>
		<PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
		<GeneratePackageOnBuild>False</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
		<OutputType>Library</OutputType>
		<ProduceReferenceAssembly>True</ProduceReferenceAssembly>
		<Title>Acumatica REST API Client</Title>
		<IncludeSymbols>True</IncludeSymbols>
		<SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
		<Authors>Dmitrii-Naumov</Authors>
		<LangVersion>9.0</LangVersion>
		<nullable>Enable</nullable>
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>True</GenerateDocumentationFile>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<PropertyGroup Condition="'$(Configuration)|$(Platform)'=='Debug|AnyCPU'">
		<Optimize>False</Optimize>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<PropertyGroup Condition="'$(Configuration)|$(Platform)'=='Release|AnyCPU'">
		<Optimize>True</Optimize>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="AcumaticaRESTClientLogo.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="..\README.md">
			<Pack>True</Pack>
			<PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
		</None>
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="Newtonsoft.Json" Version="13.0.1" />
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.NetAnalyzers" Version="9.0.0">
			<PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
		</PackageReference>
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<None Update="AcumaticaRESTClientLogo.png">
			<Pack>True</Pack>
			<PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
		</None>
		<None Update="images\AcumaticaRESTClientLogo.png">
			<Pack>True</Pack>
			<PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
		</None>
	</ItemGroup>

</Project>
